35,2,1,talk,Mio,,It's sad that people sweated it out in July just to avoid arguments. But paying ahead seems to make people feel much more relaxed about using power.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The bills fluctuate wildly, from 9,000 to nearly 30,000 yen. Also, installing individual meters would be very expensive, costing 34,000 yen per room.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Rin,,Both the template and the other house's system seem like a nightmare. It takes way too much time to log everything and issue demands.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,"My suspicions were right. Some rooms use four times more power than others, and the room layout makes heating needs totally unfair.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Misaki,,The payment log shows we're already struggling. People are paying late because they're questioning the amounts. It's creating a lot of tension.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Mio,,"@Ryuji, if the bills change that much, no wonder we're stressed. We need something that stops the monthly shock.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Shunichi, if the usage is that unbalanced, a flat split is logically unfair, but the upfront cost for meters is too high.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shunichi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Rin,,"@Misaki, if people are already arguing, making the math more complex with meters or templates will just make it worse.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@Ryuji, exactly. We can't ignore that some of us are paying for others' desktop computers and heaters.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Rin, I agree. We need a solution that is simple enough that it doesn't require a ""manager"" who everyone ends up hating.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Mio,,What if we just agreed on a set amount for the season? That way we don't have to think about it every time we flip a switch.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"A seasonal fixed rate would stabilize the monthly cost, but we'd still have to settle the difference at the end of the year.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Rin,,"As long as that year-end settle isn't a huge project, it sounds better than doing it every single month.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"It doesn't solve the unfairness of room usage, but it's better than the current chaos.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Misaki,,It removes the monthly friction. That's the most important thing for the atmosphere of the house.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Mio,,"I really think the ""paying ahead"" vibe is what we need to feel at home here.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"I can accept a fixed rate if it prevents the ""second rent"" feeling in winter.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Rin,,I'm on board if it means less time spent on spreadsheets.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,I'll concede on the usage imbalance if it means we stop the bickering.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Misaki,,I agree. Let's go for the most peaceful option.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
